      "synthesis": {
        "main_text_has_explicit_synthesis": true,
        "si_used": false,
        "procedure": "Route 2 (Ln = Pr): LnCl3·xH2O was dissolved in methanol (3 mL) and combined with a methanol standard solution (0.2 M) of [Bu4N][3-NO2Tp] in a sealed 2 dram vial at a 1:2 Ln3+:ligand mol ratio. Hexanes (3 mL) were layered on the methanol mixture. Single crystals formed after 24 h; the product was isolated after 2–4 weeks by vacuum filtration, washed with 3 × 5 mL methanol, and dried under vacuum for 3–5 min. Green rod-shaped crystals of 5-Pr were isolated from methanol/hexanes. Ligand stock solutions were prepared by dissolving each [Bu4N][3-NO2Tp] batch in 20 mL methanol; the lanthanide salt amount was adjusted to the target ratio.",
